# Git Worktree Rules

## Do not create worktrees unless asked

**Never** create a git worktree (e.g. `git worktree add`) on your own. If new work needs a separate branch, create the branch in the current working directory (`git switch -c …` off the appropriate base). Only create a worktree when the user explicitly asks for one (e.g. "make a worktree", "in a new worktree", "use a worktree").

## When the user does ask for a worktree

Always run the worktree setup script **from within the new worktree directory** as a follow-up step:

```bash
bash .cursor/worktree-setup.sh
```

This script copies local agent rules, `.env` files, and installs dependencies. Do not skip it.
